Include:

Purpose & scope

Roles (IT owner, approver)

Patch schedule (Weekly check + monthly full rollouts)

Windows example: How to check Windows Update (click path: Start → Settings → Update & Security → Windows Update → Check for updates).

Linux example: commands:

Ubuntu/Debian:

sudo apt update
sudo apt -y upgrade


RHEL/CentOS:

sudo yum update


Rollout approach: test on two machines → approve → push via Windows WSUS or scripting

Evidence & verification: export update history or screenshot

Emergency patching process

Sample policy line:

Policy: Security updates should be validated and applied to all workstations within 14 calendar days of release, except where testing indicates a critical incompatibility. All patch operations must be logged and a screenshot of successful update applied (or an update log) uploaded to evidence folder.
